# Line endings are LF in this repository, everywhere, always.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Step 7 was written on Windows through a OneDrive-synced
# folder, and 26 files came back rewritten with CRLF. Every blob already in git
# used LF, so `git diff` reported those files as changed end to end: 16,512 lines
# of churn hiding 2,810 lines of real work. A diff nobody can read is a diff
# nobody reviews, and `git blame` on ten untouched files would have pointed at
# this commit forever.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means git normalises to LF when it stores a file and checks
# it out as LF, whatever the editor writes locally. Node, Vite and every browser
# read LF fine on Windows, so nothing downstream cares.
#
# If a whole-file diff ever appears again, the fix is:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
